  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "The colour scale a panel prints beside its field. Declared as one object because nine loose `colorbar_*` options were nine chances to style a bar that is not drawn, and because a tick list written in an options bag is not a list of numbers to anything that reads it.\n\nA heatmap carries one unasked, since it is unreadable without one; a scatter shaded by a third quantity asks with `show: true`, because a row of them conventionally shares ONE bar. `kind: colorbar` is the standalone form — a bar occupying its own cell of the mosaic, keying the panels around it, and the only case that states its own `colormap` and limits rather than taking them from the field it sits beside."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/ColoredNoise",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Coloured noise"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/Stochasticity"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/Colormaps",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "Colormaps"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid668"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid671"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid674"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid675"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid676"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid677"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Continuous colour scales, by key: anything ordinal or continuous draws from one of these, anything categorical draws from `Palette.palette`, and an ordinal scale drawn as discrete swatches samples one rather than picking hues that imply no order. A value is either a registered colormap name (`viridis`) or the list of colours to ramp between (`['#000000', '#ffffff']`). The namespace is open — a project adds its own keys for the scales it distinguishes (`bold: viridis, meg: plasma, eeg: cividis`) and names them anywhere a colormap is named. `sequential` and `diverging` are the two the renderer reaches for on its own, so they are typed here and always present: a project that declares neither still has both. An open namespace cannot catch a misspelt key — `sequentiel` is read as a project key, not as a typo — which is the price of letting a project name its own scales. A key that shadows a registered colormap name is refused, so a name cannot mean two things at once."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure"
  } ]
}, {
