  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Which matplotlib layout engine positions the mosaic's axes. Unset lets the backend pick (bsplot asks for 'compressed' and falls back to 'tight'), which is right for a plain grid of plots. A figure whose panels carry their own absolute geometry — a schematic stepped out in axes fractions, or a mosaic dense enough that the constrained solver reports cells collapsed to zero and silently falls back — has to say so, because an engine that gives up still leaves the figure laid out by a fallback nobody declared."
  } ],
