  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "The node slots a network's `node_template` sets on every node it does not set them on itself: what a node is and how it runs, and nothing that says which node it is. It shares these slots with `Node` and lacks the per-node slots `id`, `label`, `position` and `region`, which the network's data gives each node; a template that sets one is refused, naming it."
  } ],
