  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Each stage keeps its own best iterate and restores it before the next stage starts, so every stage restarts from the best state the previous one found; the run records one iteration and value per stage. This is the authors' released feedback-inhibition protocol, where each stage was a separate process that restarted from the previous stage's best checkpoint."
