  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Which iterate of an online tuning run hands its parameters to the post-tuning evaluation and to the algorithms that depend on it. Absent, the final iterate does. Declared, the loop keeps the tuned parameters and the settled state of the iteration whose criterion was best, tracked across every stage jointly and restored after the last stage (or per stage under `scope: stage`); the run records the chosen iteration and its criterion value. This is the published feedback-inhibition simulator's practice of keeping the weights of the iteration with the lowest in-loop FC error rather than the last ones."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch" : [ {
