  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Draw an arrow POINTING AT (x, y), starting (dx, dy) away from it in axes fractions — e.g. [-0.08, 0.06] for one coming from the upper left. The text, when non-empty, sits at the tail. This is how a paper's callout arrowheads are declared instead of drawn in code."
