}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/GastSchmidtKnosche_SD",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description" : [ {
    "@value" : "4D model describing the Ott-Antonsen reduction of infinite all-to-all \n    coupled QIF neurons (Theta-neurons) with Synaptic Depression adaptation \n    mechanisms [Gastetal_2020]_.\n\n    The two state variables :math:`r` and :math:`V` represent the average firing rate and \n    the average membrane potential of our QIF neurons.\n    :math:`A` and :math:`B` are respectively the adaptation variable and its derivative.\n\n    The equations of the infinite QIF 2D population model read\n    \n    .. math::\n            \\dot{r} &= 1/\\tau (\\Delta/(\\pi \\tau) + 2 V r)\\\\\n            \\dot{V} &= 1/\\tau (V^2 - \\tau^2 \\pi^2 r^2 + \\eta + J \\tau r (1 - A) + I)\\\\ \n            \\dot{A} &= 1/\\tau_A (B)\\\\\n            \\dot{B} &= 1/\\tau_A (-2 B - A + \\alpha  r) \\\\\n\n    .. [Gastetal_2020] Gast, R., Schmidt, H., & Knösche, T. R. (2020). A mean-field description of bursting dynamics in spiking neural networks with short-term adaptation. *Neural Computation*, 32(9), 1615-1634."
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Gast2020"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/Dynamics"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "GastSchmidtKnosche_SD"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Gast-Schmidt-Knosche (synaptic depression)"
  } ],
  "https://w3id.org/tvbo/exhibitsBifurcation" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid5066"
  } ],
